		{
			dependencies: ["6C0C75598D65CE7D"]
			description: [
				"The &eConfigurator&r is Mekanism's wrench, and it does far more than turn blocks."
				""
				"&e&lCycle its mode with the mode key&r (default &bM&r while holding it):"
				"&7- &fConfigure&7 - recolour a machine's sides for input/output. This is the mode you will live in."
				"&7- &fEmpty&7 - drain a machine's internal tanks and buffers."
				"&7- &fRotate&7 - turn a block without breaking it."
				"&7- &fWrench&7 - pick a machine up whole, keeping its inventory and settings."
				""
				"&c&lAlmost every 'my machine does nothing' problem is a side config problem.&r A machine face set to the wrong colour will not accept input or push output. Open the machine's side-config tab and match the colours to what your pipes expect."
				""
				"&8Craft this before your second machine, not after your tenth."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:configurator"
			id: "7ADE000000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000001"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Rotate, wrench, empty, configure"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000100"
				item: "mekanism:configurator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Configurator"
			x: -11.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000001"]
			description: [
				"&eUniversal Cables&r move Forge Energy between anything - Mekanism machines, Powah reactors, AE2 acceptors, all of it."
				""
				"&e&lFour tiers, each moving far more per tick:&r &7Basic &8→ &7Advanced &8→ &7Elite &8→ &7Ultimate&r. Upgrade in place with the tier installers."
				""
				"&c&lThroughput is the thing that catches people.&r A Basic cable feeding an Ultimate Factory is a bottleneck you cannot see - the machine simply runs slowly and looks broken. If a machine is starved, check the cable tier before you build another generator."
				""
				"&7Cables have a small internal buffer, so a long run behaves like a tiny battery. That is usually helpful, but it means a freshly-placed line takes a moment to fill before machines spin up.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_universal_cable"
			id: "7ADE000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000002"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Energy, tiered"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000200"
				item: "mekanism:basic_universal_cable"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Universal Cables"
			x: -11.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000001"]
			description: [
				"&eMechanical Pipes&r carry fluids - water to your Electrolytic Separator, lava to your generators, brine across an evaporation plant."
				""
				"&e&lSet the pull side with the Configurator.&r A pipe touching a tank does nothing until one end is set to pull. This is the single most common fluid-logistics mistake."
				""
				"&e&lTiers matter more here than with cables&r because fluid recipes consume in large gulps. A Basic pipe will not keep a Thermal Evaporation Plant fed."
				""
				"&7Pipes will happily mix fluids if two sources feed the same network and it will jam. Keep one fluid per pipe network, or use the Configurator to colour-separate them.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_mechanical_pipe"
			id: "7ADE000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000003"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Fluids"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000300"
				item: "mekanism:basic_mechanical_pipe"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Mechanical Pipes"
			x: -11.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000002"]
			description: [
				"&ePressurised Tubes&r carry gases: oxygen, hydrogen, chlorine, sulfuric acid, polonium and the rest."
				""
				"&c&lGases do not travel in item pipes, fluid pipes or cables.&r They need these specifically. Every 'my Purification Chamber will not run' report comes down to oxygen having no route."
				""
				"&e&lBuffer with a Chemical Tank.&r Gas production is bursty and consumption is steady. A tank between the two stops your Electrolytic Separator throttling itself every time the chamber pauses."
				""
				"&7Same four tiers as everything else. Gas throughput becomes a real constraint once you are running the 4x and 5x ore chains simultaneously.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_pressurized_tube"
			id: "7ADE000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000004"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Gases - their own plumbing"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000400"
				item: "mekanism:basic_pressurized_tube"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Pressurised Tubes"
			x: -9.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000003"]
			description: [
				"&eLogistical Transporters&r are Mekanism's item pipes - and unlike hoppers they are genuinely smart."
				""
				"&e&lItems travel to a destination that will accept them&r, and bounce back to their origin if nothing will. Nothing voids, nothing jams on a full chest."
				""
				"&e&lThe variants are worth knowing:&r"
				"&7- &fLogistical Transporter&7 - the normal item pipe."
				"&7- &fRestrictive&7 - only used as a last resort, so you can build an overflow path."
				"&7- &fDiversion&7 - redstone-controlled on/off. Route switching without rebuilding."
				""
				"&8Combine with the Logistical Sorter in the next quest and you have a full sorting system with no mod other than Mekanism."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_logistical_transporter"
			id: "7ADE000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000005"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Items that route themselves"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000500"
				item: "mekanism:basic_logistical_transporter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Logistical Transporters"
			x: -9.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000005"]
			description: [
				"A &eLogistical Sorter&r sits on the output face of a machine or chest and pushes items into a transporter network by filter."
				""
				"&e&lFilter types:&r"
				"&7- &fItem&7 - a specific item."
				"&7- &fTag&7 - everything matching a tag, e.g. all ingots."
				"&7- &fMaterial&7 - everything made of one material."
				"&7- &fMod ID&7 - everything from one mod. Enormously useful for bulk sorting."
				""
				"&e&lColour-coding is the clever part.&r Assign a colour to a filter and only transporters set to that colour will carry it. One physical pipe run can carry several logical routes."
				""
				"&7Set 'Auto Eject' on the machine and the sorter does the rest. This is how you turn a wall of machines into a factory that feeds itself.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:logistical_sorter"
			id: "7ADE000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000006"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Filtered output, colour-coded"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000600"
				item: "mekanism:logistical_sorter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Logistical Sorter"
			x: -9.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000006"]
			description: [
				"&eThermodynamic Conductors&r move &lheat&r - the fourth thing Mekanism pipes, after energy, fluids and gases."
				""
				"&e&lHeat matters for two systems:&r the &7Thermoelectric Boiler&r, which needs heat delivered to boil water, and the &7Fission Reactor&r, which needs heat carried away before it melts down."
				""
				"&c&lThat second one is not optional.&r An under-cooled fission reactor in this pack will destroy your base. Conductors are part of the safety system, not a nicety."
				""
				"&7You can also run them from a Resistive Heater to boil water with pure electricity - inefficient, but it works anywhere and needs no fuel.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_thermodynamic_conductor"
			id: "7ADE000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000007"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Heat is a resource here"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000700"
				item: "mekanism:basic_thermodynamic_conductor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Thermodynamic Conductors"
			x: -11.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ECDAF64265C939E"]
			description: [
				"The &eChemical Dissolution Chamber&r dissolves ore in &7sulfuric acid&r, producing a dirty slurry. This is step one of &a5x&r ore processing."
				""
				"&e&lThe full 5x chain, five machines deep:&r"
				"&71.&r &fDissolution Chamber&7 - ore + sulfuric acid &8→&7 dirty slurry"
				"&72.&r &fChemical Washer&7 - dirty slurry + water &8→&7 clean slurry"
				"&73.&r &fChemical Crystallizer&7 - clean slurry &8→&7 crystal"
				"&74.&r &fEnrichment Chamber&7 - crystal &8→&7 shard, then dust"
				"&75.&r &fEnergized Smelter&7 - dust &8→&7 ingot"
				""
				"&e&lSulfuric acid needs its own production line:&r sulfur dioxide from the &7Chemical Oxidizer&r, then the &7Chemical Infuser&r. Build that before this machine or it sits idle."
				""
				"&8Five ingots per ore. It is a lot of infrastructure for a 25% gain over 4x - build it because you want the factory, not because you need the ore."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:chemical_dissolution_chamber"
			id: "7ADE000000000008"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000008"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Start of the 5x chain"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000800"
				item: "mekanism:chemical_dissolution_chamber"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Chemical Dissolution Chamber"
			x: 1.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000008"]
			description: [
				"The &eChemical Washer&r takes the dirty slurry from the Dissolution Chamber and washes it with water into clean slurry."
				""
				"&e&lIt drinks water continuously.&r Feed it from an Electric Pump on an infinite source rather than hauling buckets - this machine will out-consume anything you do by hand."
				""
				"&7Both slurries are gases, so everything in and out of this machine travels by Pressurised Tube. If it looks stuck, check the tube run before the machine.&r"
				""
				"&8Slurry is per-metal. Iron slurry and gold slurry are different gases, and mixing their tube networks will jam both. Colour-code with the Configurator or run separate lines."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:chemical_washer"
			id: "7ADE000000000009"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000009"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Dirty slurry into clean"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000900"
				item: "mekanism:chemical_washer"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Chemical Washer"
			x: 3.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000009"]
			description: [
				"The &eChemical Crystallizer&r turns clean slurry back into a solid - an ore crystal, ready to re-enter the machines you already own."
				""
				"&e&lThis is where the chain rejoins familiar ground.&r Crystal into the Enrichment Chamber gives you shards, then dust, then the Energized Smelter finishes the job. The last two machines are the same ones you built in First Machines."
				""
				"&a&lWith all five stages running you are at 5x&r - five ingots from one ore chunk, the ceiling of Mekanism ore processing."
				""
				"&7Automate the hand-offs with Logistical Transporters and a Sorter. A 5x line moved by hand is not worth building.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:chemical_crystallizer"
			id: "7ADE00000000000A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000000A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Slurry back into solids"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000A00"
				item: "mekanism:chemical_crystallizer"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Chemical Crystallizer"
			x: 5.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000000A"]
			description: [
				"The &eThermal Evaporation Plant&r is a multiblock tower that boils water into &7brine&r, and brine into &7lithium&r."
				""
				"&e&lThe build:&r a hollow tower of Thermal Evaporation Blocks with a Controller, valves for input and output, and height. &lTaller is faster&r - the plant's speed scales with how many layers you stack."
				""
				"&e&lSpeed also scales with heat and sunlight.&r Put it under open sky, or feed it heat from a Resistive Heater or Fuelwood Heater through Thermodynamic Conductors."
				""
				"&e&lWhat it feeds:&r lithium is the input for the &7Isotopic Centrifuge&r and the fusion line, and brine is needed for sodium and chlorine. This is the gateway to Mekanism's late chemistry."
				""
				"&8It is slow. Build it early and let it run in the background while you do other things - it does not need attention, only time."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:thermal_evaporation_controller"
			id: "7ADE00000000000B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000000B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Brine, lithium, and a big build"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000B00"
				item: "mekanism:thermal_evaporation_controller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Thermal Evaporation Plant"
			x: 7.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["742152612BC35B66"]
			description: [
				"The &eChemical Infuser&r combines two gases into a third. It is the heart of Mekanism's chemistry."
				""
				"&e&lThe combinations you will actually use:&r"
				"&7- &fHydrogen + Chlorine&7 &8→&7 &fHydrogen Chloride&7 - the 4x ore chain"
				"&7- &fSulfur Dioxide + Oxygen&7 &8→&7 &fSulfur Trioxide&7"
				"&7- &fSulfur Trioxide + Water Vapour&7 &8→&7 &fSulfuric Acid&7 - the 5x ore chain"
				"&7- &fDeuterium + Tritium&7 &8→&7 &fD-T Fuel&7 - fusion"
				""
				"&c&lNote the sulfuric acid chain runs through this machine twice.&r Build two rather than trying to time-share one, or your 5x line will stall constantly."
				""
				"&7Every input and output is a gas, so this whole area of your base is Pressurised Tubes and Chemical Tanks.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:chemical_infuser"
			id: "7ADE00000000000C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000000C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Two gases into one"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000C00"
				item: "mekanism:chemical_infuser"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Chemical Infuser"
			x: -5.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000000C"]
			description: [
				"The &ePRC&r takes an item, a fluid and a gas simultaneously and produces an item and a gas. It is the most demanding machine to plumb in the mod."
				""
				"&e&lWhat it makes that you care about:&r"
				"&7- &fSubstrate&7 - from bio fuel, water and hydrogen. Feeds HDPE."
				"&7- &fHDPE&7 - Mekanism's plastic, in everything late-tier."
				"&7- &fFissile Fuel&7 - from polonium. This is the fission reactor's food."
				""
				"&c&lThree different input types means three different pipe systems converging on one block.&r Plan the space before you place it - retrofitting pipes around a PRC is miserable."
				""
				"&7Bio Fuel comes from your Crusher fed with surplus saplings, which you already have in quantity from the Crook.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:pressurized_reaction_chamber"
			id: "7ADE00000000000D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000000D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Item + fluid + gas at once"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000D00"
				item: "mekanism:pressurized_reaction_chamber"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Pressurised Reaction Chamber"
			x: -3.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000000D"]
			description: [
				"The &eRotary Condensentrator&r converts a gas into its fluid form or the reverse, toggled with a button on its GUI."
				""
				"&e&lWhy you need it:&r some machines want liquid, some want gas, and Mekanism is strict about it. Liquid oxygen, liquid chlorine and liquid hydrogen all exist and all have uses - this block is the translator."
				""
				"&c&lCheck the direction toggle first.&r A condensentrator set the wrong way looks exactly like a broken machine: it takes input and produces nothing."
				""
				"&7Also the practical way to &lstore&r gas in bulk - convert to fluid, park it in a Dynamic Tank, convert back on demand. Fluid storage is far cheaper than gas storage.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:rotary_condensentrator"
			id: "7ADE00000000000E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000000E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Gas to fluid, and back"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000E00"
				item: "mekanism:rotary_condensentrator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Rotary Condensentrator"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000000C"]
			description: [
				"The &eIsotopic Centrifuge&r separates isotopes - most importantly turning deuterium into &7tritium&r."
				""
				"&e&lThe fusion fuel chain:&r"
				"&7Water &8→&7 &fElectrolytic Separator&7 &8→&7 heavy water &8→&7 &fCentrifuge&7 &8→&7 deuterium &8→&7 &fCentrifuge&7 &8→&7 tritium&r"
				"&7Then deuterium + tritium &8→&7 &fChemical Infuser&7 &8→&7 &fD-T Fuel&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt is deliberately slow.&r Fusion is meant to be an infrastructure project, not a crafting recipe. Run several centrifuges in parallel and let them accumulate."
				""
				"&8Also produces plutonium and polonium from nuclear waste, which is how the Ascension chapter's antimatter line begins."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:isotopic_centrifuge"
			id: "7ADE00000000000F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000000F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Toward fusion"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000000F00"
				item: "mekanism:isotopic_centrifuge"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Isotopic Centrifuge"
			x: -5.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000000D"]
			description: [
				"An &eElectric Pump&r sits in a fluid source and pumps it into your pipe network indefinitely."
				""
				"&e&lThis is what makes the whole chemistry tree practical.&r The Electrolytic Separator, Chemical Washer and Thermal Evaporation Plant all drink water continuously. Carrying buckets is not a strategy."
				""
				"&e&lWith a Filter Upgrade&r it becomes a &7heavy water&r extractor - drawing the trace heavy water out of an ordinary water source. That is the first step of the fusion fuel chain."
				""
				"&7Pumps lava too, which pairs neatly with a Thermo Generator bank or an obsidian line.&r"
				""
				"&8One pump on an infinite water source will supply an entire base. Build it early."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:electric_pump"
			id: "7ADE000000000010"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000010"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Infinite water, no buckets"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001000"
				item: "mekanism:electric_pump"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Electric Pump"
			x: -3.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000000E"]
			description: [
				"A &eChemical Tank&r buffers gas; a &eFluid Tank&r buffers liquid. Both are portable and keep their contents when broken."
				""
				"&c&lBuffers are not optional in Mekanism.&r Production is bursty, consumption is steady, and a machine with nowhere to put its output &lstops&r. One tank between every producer and consumer removes an entire category of problem."
				""
				"&e&lThe portable part is underrated.&r A filled tank in your inventory is how you carry oxygen to a Moon base, or move a stock of hydrogen to a new build without piping across the island."
				""
				"&7For serious volume, the &fDynamic Tank&r multiblock scales to whatever size you build it - far cheaper per bucket than stacking single tanks.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:basic_chemical_tank"
			id: "7ADE000000000011"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000011"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Stop your chemistry stalling"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7AE0000000001100"
					item: "mekanism:basic_chemical_tank"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7AE0000000001101"
					item: "mekanism:basic_fluid_tank"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Tanks & Buffers"
			x: -1.0d
			y: -6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0FBFBB69863D68E7"]
			description: [
				"The &eQIO Drive Array&r holds QIO drives - Mekanism's answer to AE2, built entirely from things you already make."
				""
				"&e&lQIO versus AE2, honestly:&r"
				"&7- &fNo channels, no cables, no controller.&7 Components just need to be near each other."
				"&7- &fFar simpler to set up&7 - a Drive Array, a Dashboard, done."
				"&7- &fNo autocrafting.&7 This is the real trade. QIO stores; AE2 crafts."
				""
				"&e&lIt is genuinely useful alongside AE2&r, not instead of it - QIO for bulk material overflow, AE2 for the crafting brain."
				""
				"&7Drives come in four tiers and, unlike AE2 cells, hold a sane number of item types at every tier.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:qio_drive_array"
			id: "7ADE000000000012"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000012"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mekanism's own storage network"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001200"
				item: "mekanism:qio_drive_array"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9QIO Drive Array"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000012"]
			description: [
				"The &eQIO Dashboard&r is your window into the QIO network - search, withdraw, insert, and a crafting grid attached."
				""
				"&e&lThere is also a &fPortable QIO Dashboard&e&l item&r that gives you the same access from your inventory anywhere in range of the network. No wireless terminal, no access point, no boosters."
				""
				"&e&lFrequencies work like the Entangloporter's&r - name a frequency, set every QIO component to it, and they are one system. Private frequencies keep other players out on a shared server."
				""
				"&7The Dashboard also feeds the Formulaic Assemblicator, which is as close to autocrafting as QIO gets.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:qio_dashboard"
			id: "7ADE000000000013"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000013"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Search and pull, no channels"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001300"
				item: "mekanism:qio_dashboard"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9QIO Dashboard"
			x: 9.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000013"]
			description: [
				"&eQIO Importers&r pull items from a machine into the network; &eExporters&r push them back out. Same idea as AE2's buses, without the channel budget."
				""
				"&e&lBoth take filters&r, so you can pull only the outputs you want and feed only the inputs a machine needs."
				""
				"&e&lThe &fQIO Redstone Adapter&e&r is the piece people miss:&r it emits a redstone signal when a chosen item drops below a set count. Wire that to a machine and you have automatic restocking with no computer and no crafting card."
				""
				"&8That trio - Importer, Exporter, Redstone Adapter - is a complete factory automation loop using nothing but Mekanism."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:qio_importer"
			id: "7ADE000000000014"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000014"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Automate the network"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7AE0000000001400"
					item: "mekanism:qio_importer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7AE0000000001401"
					item: "mekanism:qio_exporter"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9QIO Importers & Exporters"
			x: 9.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000013"]
			description: [
				"The &eFormulaic Assemblicator&r stores a crafting recipe as a &7Crafting Formula&r and repeats it forever from piped-in materials."
				""
				"&e&lHow to set one up:&r"
				"&71.&r Craft a blank &7Crafting Formula&r."
				"&72.&r Put it in the Assemblicator with the recipe laid out in the grid."
				"&73.&r Encode it. The formula now remembers that recipe."
				"&74.&r Feed materials in and it produces continuously."
				""
				"&e&lThis is Mekanism's autocrafting&r - one recipe per machine, rather than AE2's request-anything network. For high-volume repeats like circuits, alloys or casings it is arguably better: no CPU to tie up, no craft to queue, it simply always has stock."
				""
				"&7Pair with a QIO Importer on the output and your circuit supply solves itself.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:formulaic_assemblicator"
			id: "7ADE000000000015"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000015"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Repeat crafting, automated"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001500"
				item: "mekanism:formulaic_assemblicator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Formulaic Assemblicator"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19236F17F30F94C7"]
			description: [
				"A &eResistive Heater&r turns Forge Energy directly into heat. Inefficient, entirely controllable, and it works anywhere."
				""
				"&e&lWhy bother when lava is free?&r Because heat output here is a &lnumber you set&r. A boiler fed by lava is at the mercy of your lava supply; a boiler fed by resistive heaters produces exactly as much steam as you tell it to."
				""
				"&e&lIt is the standard way to drive a Thermoelectric Boiler&r when you have surplus power and want it as steam for a turbine - which sounds circular until you are load-balancing a fission plant."
				""
				"&7Also the simplest heat source for a Thermal Evaporation Plant that is not getting enough sun.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:resistive_heater"
			id: "7ADE000000000016"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000016"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Electricity into heat"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001600"
				item: "mekanism:resistive_heater"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Resistive Heater"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000016"]
			description: [
				"The &eThermoelectric Boiler&r is a multiblock that turns heat and water into steam. It is half of Mekanism's serious power generation."
				""
				"&e&lThe build:&r a hollow box of Boiler Casing with &7Pressure Disperser&r plates dividing water below from steam above, a &7Superheating Element&r for each heat source, and valves for input and output."
				""
				"&e&lIts output is steam, not power.&r The boiler makes steam; an &7Industrial Turbine&r turns steam into FE. Neither is useful without the other, so plan to build both together."
				""
				"&c&lSize it to your heat source.&r An oversized boiler with two superheating elements produces no more steam than a small one - it just cost more. Check the boiler's stats screen, which tells you its maximum boil rate."
				""
				"&8This is the block your Fission Reactor will feed in Ascension. Building it now with resistive heaters is good practice at low stakes."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:boiler_casing"
			id: "7ADE000000000017"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000017"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Water into steam, at scale"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001700"
				item: "mekanism:boiler_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Thermoelectric Boiler"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000017"]
			description: [
				"The &eIndustrial Turbine&r is a multiblock that converts steam into Forge Energy - and at full size it produces more power than anything else in the pack short of fusion."
				""
				"&e&lThe build, from the bottom up:&r a Turbine Casing shell, a &7Turbine Rotor&r column up the centre with &7Turbine Blades&r on it, &7Pressure Dispersers&r above, a &7Rotational Complex&r, coils, and vents to release spent steam."
				""
				"&e&lMore blades and more vents means more throughput.&r The turbine's own stats screen tells you its maximum flow rate and whether your vents are limiting it - read it rather than guessing."
				""
				"&c&lVents are the usual bottleneck.&r A turbine that will not hit its rated output almost always needs more vents, not more blades."
				""
				"&7Pair with the boiler above and an Induction Matrix to store the output, and your power problems are over for the rest of the pack.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:turbine_casing"
			id: "7ADE000000000018"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000018"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Steam into serious power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001800"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:turbine_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Industrial Turbine"
			x: -3.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000018"]
			description: [
				"The &eGas-Burning Generator&r burns combustible gas - most usefully the &7hydrogen&r your Electrolytic Separator is already producing as a by-product."
				""
				"&e&lThis closes a loop you already have open.&r You are splitting water for oxygen to feed the Purification Chamber. The hydrogen half is usually vented or ignored. Feed it here instead and your ore chain part-funds its own power."
				""
				"&e&lIt also burns ethene&r, which the PRC makes from bio fuel - so surplus saplings become electricity through a slightly longer road."
				""
				"&7Buffer the gas with a Chemical Tank. Feeding a generator directly from a separator means both stall whenever either hiccups.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanismgenerators:gas_burning_generator"
			id: "7ADE000000000019"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000019"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Burn hydrogen for power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001900"
				item: "mekanismgenerators:gas_burning_generator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Gas-Burning Generator"
			x: -1.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["21557404ADD43A57"]
			description: [
				"The &eModification Station&r installs modules into MekaSuit pieces and the Meka-Tool. Without it the suit is just expensive armour."
				""
				"&e&lModules are the whole point of the MekaSuit.&r A short list of the ones that change how you play:"
				"&7- &fJetpack Unit&7 - flight, on the chestplate"
				"&7- &fGravitational Modulating Unit&7 - proper creative-style flight, late"
				"&7- &fInhalation Purification&7 - immunity to most status effects"
				"&7- &fElytra Unit&7 - gliding without an elytra"
				"&7- &fVein Mining&7 and &fFarming&7 units on the Meka-Tool - mine a whole ore vein or till a field in one click"
				"&7- &fTeleportation Unit&7 - short-range blink"
				""
				"&c&lModules cost power from the suit&r, and several running at once will drain it fast. An Energy Cube or a charger at base is not optional."
				""
				"&8Install modules one at a time and try them. Some conflict, and the station will tell you."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:modification_station"
			id: "7ADE00000000001A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000001A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Where MekaSuit becomes yours"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001A00"
				item: "mekanism:modification_station"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Modification Station"
			x: 3.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000001A"]
			description: [
				"The &eRobit&r is a small robot that follows you around, picks up drops, and carries a crafting table and a furnace inside it."
				""
				"&e&lWhat it is genuinely good for:&r a portable crafting grid and item pickup while you are out mining or exploring, without going home. It also fights, badly."
				""
				"&e&lIt needs charging&r at a &7Chargepad&r, and it will follow you into other dimensions."
				""
				"&7Name it. It keeps the name, and it is the only thing in this pack that will follow you to Venus voluntarily.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:robit"
			id: "7ADE00000000001B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000001B"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7A follower that crafts and fetches"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001B00"
				item: "mekanism:robit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9The Robit"
			x: 5.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000001B"]
			description: [
				"The &eSecurity Desk&r sets access rules on every Mekanism machine you own - public, trusted-players-only, or private."
				""
				"&e&lOn a shared server this is worth ten minutes of setup.&r Without it, anything you build is open to anyone who wanders past, including your Induction Matrix and your fission reactor controls."
				""
				"&7Add trusted players by name and they can use your machines without being able to reconfigure them.&r"
				""
				"&8Also protects Entangloporter and Teleporter frequencies, which are otherwise a genuinely open door into your base."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:security_desk"
			id: "7ADE00000000001C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000001C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Lock your machines"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001C00"
				item: "mekanism:security_desk"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Security Desk"
			x: 3.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000001B"]
			description: [
				"A &eCardboard Box&r placed on any block picks it up &lwhole&r - contents, settings, orientation and all - and turns it into an item you can carry."
				""
				"&e&lIt works on almost anything, including blocks from other mods&r - a full AE2 drive, a chest with items still in it, a machine mid-recipe."
				""
				"&c&lThis is the single best base-moving tool in the pack.&r Rebuilding a machine room by hand is hours; boxing it is minutes."
				""
				"&7Crouch to place the box without triggering it if you just want to store boxes.&r"
				""
				"&8Craft a stack. You will use more than you expect the first time you decide your base layout was a mistake."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:cardboard_box"
			id: "7ADE00000000001D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000001D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Move a machine without losing it"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001D00"
				item: "mekanism:cardboard_box"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Cardboard Box"
			x: 5.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000001D"]
			description: [
				"The &eSeismic Vibrator&r scans the chunk it sits in and, read with a &7Seismic Reader&r, tells you exactly what blocks are in the column beneath you and at what depth."
				""
				"&e&lOn a void island this is nearly useless&r - there is nothing beneath you. Its value is entirely off-world: the Moon, Mars, Venus, Glacio and the Twilight Forest all have real terrain and real ore."
				""
				"&7Pair it with the Digital Miner. Vibrator to find out whether a spot is worth mining, Digital Miner to strip it without digging.&r"
				""
				"&8Cheap, one-off, and it saves a lot of pointless tunnelling on planets where the air is trying to kill you."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:seismic_vibrator"
			id: "7ADE00000000001E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000001E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Read the ground"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001E00"
				item: "mekanism:seismic_vibrator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Seismic Vibrator"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE00000000001E"]
			description: [
				"The &eOredictionificator&r converts an item into another item that shares the same tag - one mod's copper into another's, one variant of a resource into the one your recipe wants."
				""
				"&e&lIn a 167-mod pack this comes up constantly.&r Several mods add their own version of the same material, and recipes are often picky about which one they take. This block quietly makes the problem go away."
				""
				"&7Set the filter to the tag you want to normalise, feed the mixed items in, and get one consistent output.&r"
				""
				"&8Particularly handy downstream of the sieve, where ore chunks from different mods pile up alongside each other."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:oredictionificator"
			id: "7ADE00000000001F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF00000000001F"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Convert between equivalents"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000001F00"
				item: "mekanism:oredictionificator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Oredictionificator"
			x: 9.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000019"]
			description: [
				"A &eRadioactive Waste Barrel&r holds nuclear waste and slowly decays it away."
				""
				"&c&lThis is a safety device, and Mekanism radiation is not cosmetic.&r Waste released into the world irradiates the area, gives you lasting radiation poisoning, and does not clean itself up quickly. A leak near your base is a genuine problem."
				""
				"&e&lThe fission reactor produces waste continuously.&r You have three options: barrel it, decay it, or feed it into the &7Solar Neutron Activator&r for polonium - which the Ascension chapter needs anyway. The third is strictly better."
				""
				"&7Carry a &fGeiger Counter&r and a &fDosimeter&r before you start the fission line. One tells you how irradiated an area is, the other how irradiated &lyou&r are.&r"
				""
				"&8Never break a pipe carrying waste. Empty it with the Configurator first."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:radioactive_waste_barrel"
			id: "7ADE000000000020"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000020"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Store it or vent it"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000002000"
				item: "mekanism:radioactive_waste_barrel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Radioactive Waste Barrel"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000020"]
			description: [
				"A &eLaser&r fires a beam that breaks blocks at range, and can be chained through &7Laser Amplifiers&r to store and release enormous energy in one pulse."
				""
				"&e&lThe practical use is the &fLaser Tractor Beam&e&r, which collects everything the laser breaks and pipes it to a chest - a mining setup with no moving parts."
				""
				"&e&lThe Amplifier is the clever part.&r It charges up and fires only when it reaches a threshold you set, so a slow trickle of power becomes a beam strong enough to break blocks a plain laser could not."
				""
				"&7Lasers pass through Structural Glass, which is how you aim one out of a sealed room.&r"
				""
				"&8Mostly a toy on a void island, genuinely useful on a planet with terrain."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:laser"
			id: "7ADE000000000021"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000021"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Precision cutting, and a big battery"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000002100"
				item: "mekanism:laser"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Lasers"
			x: -5.0d
			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000021"]
			description: [
				"The &eDimensional Stabilizer&r keeps chunks loaded around it, powered by FE."
				""
				"&e&lWhy this matters more than FTB Chunks here:&r your force-load allowance is limited and shared, and it does not follow you off-world. A Stabilizer on the Moon keeps your Moon base running whether or not you have chunk claims there."
				""
				"&e&lIt costs power per chunk&r, and the cost rises with how many you load. Load the chunk the machines are in, not a comfortable radius around them."
				""
				"&c&lRemember the standing rule on this server:&r nothing that slows the machine down. Every loaded chunk ticks forever - be deliberate about which ones."
				""
				"&7Between this, FTB Chunks and the Quantum Entangloporter, an off-world outpost can run completely unattended.&r"
			]
			icon: "mekanism:dimensional_stabilizer"
			id: "7ADE000000000022"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000022"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Chunk loading, Mekanism-style"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000002200"
				item: "mekanism:dimensional_stabilizer"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Dimensional Stabilizer"
			x: -3.0d
			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ADE000000000022"]
			description: [
				"The &eFlamethrower&r burns hydrogen from your gas network - the same hydrogen the Electrolytic Separator makes as a by-product."
				""
				"&e&lThree modes&r, cycled with the mode key: &7Combat&r for burning things, &7Heat&r for smelting blocks in place, and &7Inferno&r for setting large areas alight."
				""
				"&e&lHeat mode is the interesting one&r - it smelts blocks where they stand, so you can cook a wall of ore into ingots without touching a furnace."
				""
				"&c&lIt sets you on fire as readily as anything else.&r Fire resistance, or stand well back."
				""
				"&8Refill it from any Chemical Tank of hydrogen. Free ammunition, given you are already making it."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:flamethrower"
			id: "7ADE000000000023"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000023"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Hydrogen, weaponised"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000002300"
				item: "mekanism:flamethrower"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Flamethrower"
			x: -1.0d
			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"7ADE000000000023"
				"7ADE000000000015"
				"7ADE000000000019"
				"7ADE00000000000B"
			]
			description: [
				"&9&lYou have built all of it.&r"
				""
				"Ore processing at 5x. A chemistry line making its own acids. Steam power from a boiler and turbine you sized yourself. Storage that indexes itself, crafting that repeats itself, and a suit that flies."
				""
				"&7What is left is in &fAscension &7- the fission reactor, the Solar Neutron Activator, polonium, the SPS, and two pellets of antimatter for the Heart of the Sky.&r"
				""
				"&8Everything you built here is a prerequisite for that. Nothing was wasted."
			]
			icon: "mekanism:pellet_antimatter"
			id: "7ADE000000000024"
			min_required_dependencies: 1
			rewards: [{
				id: "7ADF000000000024"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Every system, running"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7AE0000000002400"
				title: "Master Mekanism"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&9&lMaster of Mekanism"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6C0C75598D65CE7D"]
			description: [
				"&eWind Generators&r love the void - they scale with altitude, and you live at the top of the sky. Place a field of them high up for cheap, clean Mekanism power."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the one generator a skyblock is actually good at.&r Output scales with Y level, and you start higher than most players ever build. Free real estate."
				""
				"&e&lThe rules that matter:&r"
				"&7- &fOutput rises with altitude.&7 Build them on your highest platform, not at base level."
				"&7- &fThey need open sky.&7 Blocks directly above kill them."
				"&7- &fThey do not need fuel, water, or attention.&7 Ever."
				"&7- &fSome dimensions have no wind at all&7 - do not plan a Moon base around them."
				""
				"&e&lThey are individually weak.&r One will not run a Purification Chamber. The answer is quantity - a field of twenty is trivially cheap, silent, and needs nothing from you again."
				""
				"&7Wire them into an Energy Cube rather than straight to machines. Wind output is steady but small, and the buffer is what turns a trickle into something that can handle a burst of demand.&r"
				""
				"&8Cheap enough to be your first real grid, weak enough that you will still want Powah reactors later. Build both."
			]
